# Internationalization Error Handling Guidelines

## Scope / Flexibility Notice
These guidelines define standardized approaches for handling errors related to internationalization in the Flutter Chat Application. They apply to all error cases including missing translations, formatting errors, and locale-specific issues. Following these rules ensures a consistent user experience across different languages and regions.

## Best Practices
- Always provide fallback translations for critical UI elements
- Handle missing translations gracefully with fallback to default language
- Log missing translations but don't crash the application
- Validate translation parameters at runtime where feasible
- Use try-catch blocks around complex ICU message formatting
- Implement graceful degradation for unsupported locales
- Document expected behavior for missing translations
- Use a centralized error handler for translation issues
- Monitor translation errors in analytics
- Test error scenarios explicitly to verify recovery
- Provide visual feedback for recoverable errors
- Implement remote translation updates when possible

## Handling Missing Translations
- Implement a fallback chain: requested locale → default locale → hardcoded string
- Show the key name only as a last resort in development builds
- In production, never show translation keys to end users
- Consider visual indicators for untranslated strings in debug mode
- Record metrics on missing translations for later analysis
- Example:
  ```dart
  String getTranslatedText(BuildContext context, String key, {Map<String, dynamic>? args}) {
    try {
      // Try to get the translation using the generated code
      final translation = args == null 
          ? getTranslation(context, key) 
          : getTranslationWithArgs(context, key, args);
      
      // If empty or null, use fallback
      if (translation == null || translation.isEmpty) {
        return _getFallbackTranslation(context, key, args);
      }
      return translation;
    } catch (e) {
      // Log the error and provide fallback
      _logMissingTranslation(key, e);
      return _getFallbackTranslation(context, key, args) ?? 'Missing translation';
    }
  }
  
  String _getFallbackTranslation(BuildContext context, String key, Map<String, dynamic>? args) {
    // Try English locale if current is different
    if (Localizations.localeOf(context).languageCode != 'en') {
      try {
        final delegate = AppLocalizations.delegate;
        final enLocalizations = delegate.load(const Locale('en'));
        // Use reflection or a predefined mapping to find the method
        return _getTranslationFromLocalizations(enLocalizations, key, args);
      } catch (_) {
        // Fall through to next fallback
      }
    }
    
    // Return hardcoded fallback or key name in debug mode
    return kDebugMode ? '[$key]' : _hardcodedFallbacks[key] ?? key;
  }
  ```

## Parameter Validation
- Validate parameter types before formatting messages
- Handle null or invalid parameters with sensible defaults
- Use conditional formatting based on parameter values
- Example:
  ```dart
  String formatUserStatus(BuildContext context, UserStatus? status, DateTime? lastSeen) {
    // Handle null user status
    if (status == null) {
      return context.l10n.userStatusUnknown;
    }
    
    // Switch based on status with proper null handling for lastSeen
    switch (status) {
      case UserStatus.online:
        return context.l10n.userStatusOnline;
      
      case UserStatus.offline:
        if (lastSeen == null) {
          return context.l10n.userStatusOffline;
        }
        
        final now = DateTime.now();
        final difference = now.difference(lastSeen);
        
        // Format based on time difference with null checks
        if (difference.inMinutes < 1) {
          return context.l10n.userStatusJustNow;
        } else if (difference.inHours < 1) {
          return context.l10n.userStatusMinutesAgo(difference.inMinutes);
        } else {
          // Use a safe date formatter that won't crash with invalid dates
          return context.l10n.userStatusWithTime(_safeFormatTime(lastSeen));
        }
      
      case UserStatus.away:
        return context.l10n.userStatusAway;
        
      default:
        // Handle unknown status with fallback
        return context.l10n.userStatusUnknown;
    }
  }
  
  // Safe date formatter that won't crash
  String _safeFormatTime(DateTime dateTime) {
    try {
      return DateFormat.Hm().format(dateTime);
    } catch (_) {
      return "--:--";
    }
  }
  ```

## RTL/LTR Handling
- Use Directionality widgets when mixing text directions
- Test UI layout in both RTL and LTR modes
- Ensure icons and directional elements respect text direction
- Handle bidirectional text correctly with Unicode control characters when needed
- Example:
  ```dart
  Widget buildMessageBubble(BuildContext context, Message message, bool isRTL) {
    return Directionality(
      // Determine text direction based on message content or user preference
      textDirection: isRTL ? TextDirection.rtl : TextDirection.ltr,
      child: BidirectionalMessageContent(
        message: message,
        // Use start/end instead of left/right for RTL support
        padding: const EdgeInsets.only(start: 12, end: 12, top: 8, bottom: 8),
        // Adjust alignment based on direction
        alignment: isRTL ? Alignment.centerRight : Alignment.centerLeft,
        // Use safe text handling that preserves formatting
        child: Text(
          _getMessageWithEmbeddedDirectionMarkers(message.text, isRTL),
          textAlign: isRTL ? TextAlign.right : TextAlign.left,
          style: Theme.of(context).textTheme.bodyMedium,
        ),
      ),
    );
  }
  
  // Add direction markers when needed for mixed content
  String _getMessageWithEmbeddedDirectionMarkers(String text, bool isRTL) {
    // Check if text contains mixed directions that need explicit markers
    if (_containsMixedDirectionText(text)) {
      // Add Unicode direction markers for proper rendering
      return isRTL
          ? '\u200F$text\u200F' // RLM (Right-to-Left Mark)
          : '\u200E$text\u200E'; // LRM (Left-to-Right Mark)
    }
    return text;
  }
  ```

## Format-Specific Errors
- Handle date/time format errors with fallback formats
- Provide sensible defaults for number formatting issues
- Implement custom formatters for complex formatting needs
- Document expected behavior for each format type
- Example:
  ```dart
  String formatCurrency(BuildContext context, double? amount, String currencyCode) {
    if (amount == null) {
      return context.l10n.notAvailable;
    }
    
    try {
      // Try using the generated formatter with error handling
      return context.l10n.currencyFormat(amount, currencyCode);
    } catch (e) {
      // Log the error
      _logFormattingError('currencyFormat', e);
      
      try {
        // First fallback: Try using NumberFormat directly
        return NumberFormat.currency(
          symbol: currencyCode,
          decimalDigits: 2,
        ).format(amount);
      } catch (_) {
        // Second fallback: Use basic string formatting
        return '$currencyCode ${amount.toStringAsFixed(2)}';
      }
    }
  }
  
  // Safe date formatter with multiple fallback options
  String formatDate(BuildContext context, DateTime? dateTime) {
    if (dateTime == null) {
      return context.l10n.dateUnavailable;
    }
    
    try {
      // Try primary format
      return context.l10n.dateFormat(dateTime);
    } catch (e) {
      _logFormattingError('dateFormat', e);
      
      // Fallback chain with multiple options
      try {
        return DateFormat.yMd().format(dateTime);
      } catch (_) {
        try {
          return '${dateTime.year}-${dateTime.month}-${dateTime.day}';
        } catch (_) {
          return context.l10n.dateUnavailable;
        }
      }
    }
  }
  ```

## Error Recovery Strategies
- Always have a defined fallback for each error scenario
- Implement multi-level fallbacks for critical functionality
- Cache last successful translations for offline recovery
- Use static analysis to detect missing translations at build time
- Create a runtime translation verification tool for testing
- Consider user feedback mechanisms for reporting translation issues
- Example recovery workflow:
  ```dart
  Future<void> initializeLocalizations() async {
    try {
      // Try loading saved locale
      final savedLocale = await _localeStorage.getStoredLocale();
      
      // Verify the locale is available
      if (savedLocale != null && !_isLocaleSupported(savedLocale)) {
        // Log error and fall back to default
        _logger.warning('Saved locale $savedLocale is not supported, using default');
        await _localeStorage.resetToSystemLocale();
        return;
      }
      
      // Set the locale if valid
      if (savedLocale != null) {
        _localeController.add(savedLocale);
      }
    } catch (e) {
      _logger.severe('Failed to initialize localizations: $e');
      
      // Recovery: Reset to system locale and notify analytics
      await _localeStorage.resetToSystemLocale();
      _analyticsService.logEvent('localization_init_error', {
        'error_message': e.toString()
      });
    }
  }
  ```

## Testing & Validation
- Write unit tests for all error handling code
- Simulate missing translations during testing
- Test with invalid parameters and edge cases
- Verify fallback behavior works as expected
- Test RTL/LTR switching and mixed directional content
- Validate all plural forms are handled correctly
- Create visual regression tests for layout issues
- Test with incomplete translation files
- Verify localization errors are properly logged
- Simulate formatting exceptions and validate recovery
- Test with malformed locale data
- Example test:
  ```dart
  group('Localization Error Handling Tests', () {
    testWidgets('Should handle missing translation gracefully', 
      (WidgetTester tester) async {
      // Set up a test app with a modified delegate that's missing translations
      await tester.pumpWidget(
        MaterialApp(
          localizationsDelegates: [
            MockAppLocalizationsDelegate(), // Missing some translations
            GlobalMaterialLocalizations.delegate,
            GlobalWidgetsLocalizations.delegate,
          ],
          locale: const Locale('en'),
          home: const TestScreen(),
        ),
      );
      
      // Verify no exceptions are thrown
      expect(tester.takeException(), isNull);
      
      // Verify fallback text is displayed
      expect(find.text('Fallback Text'), findsOneWidget);
    });
    
    testWidgets('Should handle parameter formatting errors gracefully', 
      (WidgetTester tester) async {
      // Test with invalid date parameter
      final invalidDate = DateTime.fromMillisecondsSinceEpoch(0);
      
      await tester.pumpWidget(
        MaterialApp(
          locale: const Locale('en'),
          localizationsDelegates: const [
            AppLocalizations.delegate,
            GlobalMaterialLocalizations.delegate,
            GlobalWidgetsLocalizations.delegate,
          ],
          home: ErrorTestScreen(invalidDate: invalidDate),
        ),
      );
      
      // Verify no exceptions are thrown
      expect(tester.takeException(), isNull);
      
      // Verify fallback formatting is used
      expect(find.textContaining('1970'), findsOneWidget);
    });
  });
  ```

## Monitoring & Analysis
- Track missing translation rate in analytics
- Implement detection for repeated fallback usage
- Create a dashboard for translation coverage and errors
- Set alerts for sudden increases in translation errors
- Monitor performance impact of complex formatting
- Regularly audit logs for internationalization issues
- Implement automatic reporting of untranslated strings
- Track user-reported translation issues
- Monitor impact of locale changes on app stability
- Create periodic reports on internationalization health
- Example monitoring implementation:
  ```dart
  void _logMissingTranslation(String key, dynamic error) {
    // Log locally
    _logger.warning('Missing translation: $key, Error: $error');
    
    // Send to analytics if throttling allows
    if (_shouldReportMissingTranslation(key)) {
      _analytics.logEvent('missing_translation', {
        'key': key,
        'locale': Localizations.localeOf(context).toString(),
        'error': error.toString(),
        'timestamp': DateTime.now().toIso8601String(),
      });
      
      _recentlyReportedKeys.add(key);
      // Clean up old reports after threshold
      if (_recentlyReportedKeys.length > _maxRecentReports) {
        _recentlyReportedKeys.removeFirst();
      }
    }
  }
  ```

